  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Depthwise Separable Convolution** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cv_depthwise_separable_conv(image: list, depthwise_filter: list, pointwise_filter: list) -> list:\n    img, dw, pw = np.array(image, dtype=np.float64), np.array(depthwise_filter, dtype=np.float64), np.array(pointwise_filter, dtype=np.float64)\n    Cin, H, W = img.shape; K = dw.shape[1]; Cout = pw.shape[0]\n    oh, ow = H - K + 1, W - K + 1\n    dw_out = np.zeros((Cin, oh, ow))\n    for c in range(Cin):\n        for i in range(oh):\n            for j in range(ow):\n                dw_out[c, i, j] = np.sum(img[c, i:i+K, j:j+K] * dw[c])\n    pw_out = np.zeros((Cout, oh, ow))\n    for oc in range(Cout):\n        for ic in range(Cin):\n            pw_out[oc] += pw[oc, ic] * dw_out[ic]\n    return np.round(pw_out, 6).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
